## Lore

The CS Ranger is the Coalition military''s version of the Wilderness Scout:
less of a naturalist than the adventurer, and trained far more in tracking
human prey and guerrilla warfare. Rangers run reconnaissance, seek-and-destroy
and guerrilla missions, and hunt down deserters, escaped prisoners, refugees,
monsters, Psi-Stalkers and other Wilderness Scouts. They are cunning trap
setters who favor hit-and-run tactics.

With Special Forces, they are the soldiers most often sent deep into the
wilderness for long stretches, and one of the few who may go out alone, in a
pair, or in a group of four to six.

## GM Notes

Rangers are the most tolerant soldiers in the Coalition Army. They often team
up with D-Bees, dragons, mercenaries and practitioners of magic in the field,
and by third level most have contacts among mercenaries and outlaws - yet it
rarely shakes their loyalty, and it often helps the mission.

A reconnaissance squad or long-range patrol is typically 2-4 Rangers, 1-2
Commandos or Special Forces, 2-3 Dog Boys and a Psi-Stalker, sometimes with a
Juicer or cyborg in place of the commando. A guerrilla squad runs to about ten
and is likelier to include Juicers and an EOD Specialist.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cs-ranger');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cs-ranger';

